# Development Guidelines

## Framework Usage
- This is a SvelteKit application with Tailwind CSS
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Smart contracts are written in Rust for the Internet Computer

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript for all new JavaScript files
- Follow Svelte's component structure guidelines
- Keep components small and focused
- Use async/await for asynchronous operations
- Implement proper error handling

## State Management
- Use Svelte stores for global state
- Keep component state local when possible
- Use props for parent-child communication
- Follow unidirectional data flow

## Testing
- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Test components in isolation
- Ensure smart contract tests are comprehensive
- Follow test-driven development when possible